    {
      "title": "MS Now and CNN say their reporters were denied access to White House after Trump media ban",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/sep/19/ms-now-reporters-denied-access-white-house-trump-ban",
      "description": "<p>President said he was banning MS Now, CNN and Politico journalists, saying of their coverage: ‘You get sick of it.’</p><p>News outlets <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/media/msnbc\">MS Now</a> and CNN said their journalists were denied access to the White House grounds on Saturday morning, a day after <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump\">Donald Trump</a> said he would ban them ,and the website Politico from the executive branch complex.</p><p>MS Now said a reporter and a cameraman had been denied access and had their White House press passes confiscated by the US Secret Service at a security gate outside the West Wing. CNN reported that its reporter Betsy Klein was also denied access and had her press pass seized too.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/sep/19/ms-now-reporters-denied-access-white-house-trump-ban\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-09-19T14:39:30"
    },
    {
      "title": "Can Trump ban CNN, news outlets he doesn’t like from the White House?",
